<title>SPAIN: FOREIGN INVESTMENT IN SPAIN FALLS 24.4 PCT IN H1.</title>
<headline>FOREIGN INVESTMENT IN SPAIN FALLS 24.4 PCT IN H1.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Foreign investment in Spain fell to 656.28 billion pesetas in the first half of 1997, a 24.4 percent drop versus the same period last year, the Secretary of State for Trade's office said on Friday.</p>
<p>The European Union was the top investor with 57 percent of the total. The United States accounted for 25 percent.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585-2160</p>
</text>
